Z||000000||FieroGT 914||07-26-2001||11:24 AM||||Okay - I really need to vent on this one - Here's the story...  I found what I thought was a really great deal on an 85 2M4 Fiero a couple weeks ago in my local newspaper.  So, I went over to his place and checked it out.  I made the guy an offer on the spot and he said okay - if I want it, it's yours.  So I said yes, I want it.  Only problem was he couldn't find the title so I told him I'd wait around til he did cuz he thought it was in his safe deposit box at the bank but when he checked, it wasn't there - I know he had it but he just misplaced it and he really didn't seem shady like he was just tryin to get rid of it without a title.  It wasn't a big deal cuz I figured I'd just offer him less if he couldn't find it.  A week went by and I decided to call him last night.  Turns out the @#$*&! said he sold the car without the title and took an even bigger loss on the car (I already had it for $150).  Sucks cuz it even had a wing and decent interior parts I was gonna use when I fixed up my 87GT.  But what pisses me off is he gave me his word and then decided to sell it without even offering it to me again!  In my opinion, people like that shouldn't be associated with Fieros but that still doesn't change the fact that I got screwed out of the deal.  Oh well.<P>------------------<BR>Joe<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.worldlynx.net/asittingduck/FieroGT/Signature.jpg">  <BR>AOL I.M.: FieroGT 914<BR>White 86 1/2 GT (Stock)<BR>Maroon 87 GT (Soon to be modified and get a S/C 3800)||||reg||8
